# Credits

DicomAtlas builds on the work of the following open-source projects and
standards. Each is listed with its license and the role it plays here.

---

## Data sources

### DICOM Standard (PS3.6)
- **Publisher:** National Electrical Manufacturers Association (NEMA)
- **URL:** https://www.dicomstandard.org/current
- **Role:** Canonical source for all public tag definitions. The file
  `data/standard/attributes.json` is derived from the PS3.6 XML release.
- **License:** Open publication; see https://www.dicomstandard.org/about-dicom

### Vendor conformance statements
- **Publishers:** GE HealthCare, Siemens Healthineers, Philips Healthcare
- **Role:** Source documents for all private tag definitions. PDF manifests
  (with original and Archive.org URLs) are in `data/sources.json`.
- **Note:** Tag metadata (names, VR codes, element numbers) is factual
  technical information extracted and curated from these documents. The
  source PDFs themselves are not redistributed.

### pydicom — `_private_dict.py`
- **URL:** https://github.com/pydicom/pydicom
- **License:** MIT
- **Role:** Used as a cross-reference during the resolve step to validate VR
  assignments and backfill entries not found in the vendor PDFs. No pydicom
  source code is included in this repository; it is used only as a runtime
  validation tool during the build pipeline.

